{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd","id":1538215,"title":"How would we adapt Strahd?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-07T14:50:37-07:00","id":1538215,"title":"How would we adapt Strahd?","content":"Yes, the D&amp;D vampire.<br /> <br /> What would be a good way to make him in Dark Ages or Modern Day.<br /> <br /> Because why not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zcRKMPpsW94?list=FLfWmu27KD5LKzzySKDJidoA\" data-code=\"zcRKMPpsW94\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zcRKMPpsW94/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T17:03:03-07:00","id":1538218,"title":"","content":"So Strahd is a classic Old Clan Tzimsce, probably one of the best examples out of pop culture. In D&amp;D he has the equivalent to high levels of Dominate, Animalism and Auspex. We've seen him mind controlling people, he frequently controls the beasts and animals of Barovia, and he's exhibited the ability to notice things from all across his domain. In addition to being a Fighter, he also has high levels in wizard, so in Vampire terms, he'd have Koldunic Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T20:21:56-07:00","id":1538221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538218#post1538218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Strahd is a classic Old Clan Tzimsce, probably one of the best examples out of pop culture. In D&amp;D he has the equivalent to high levels of Dominate, Animalism and Auspex. We've seen him mind controlling people, he frequently controls the beasts and animals of Barovia, and he's exhibited the ability to notice things from all across his domain. In addition to being a Fighter, he also has high levels in wizard, so in Vampire terms, he'd have Koldunic Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the above, though I would suggest that he also knows Protean because D&amp;D vampires inherently have mist and animal forms as a species power. Unless we are modeling Strahd using Van Richtens guide to Vampires for the &quot;elder&quot; vampire stats and powers which is a whole another kettle of fish.<br /> <br /> It is worth noting that Vampires range in power depending on edition of D&amp;D used. For instance, back in 2nd Edition AD&amp;D, vampires had a touch attack called &quot;level drain&quot; which permanently destroyed xp and lowered your level per touch attack with no limit of use. The only way to get it back was to either get a specific high level priest spell cast on you or you had to re-grind all the xp to regain the levels. Being an undead hunter in 2nd Edition was bit more hardcore than other game systems.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, a VtM version of level drain would probably be something that causes permanent Willpower loss on top of ability/attribute dot loss. Something along the lines of &quot;Rune of Singular Hate&quot; from the exalted sorcery comes to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T22:11:59-07:00","id":1538224,"title":"","content":"D&amp;D level drain for undead was an artifact of the game designers wanting players to fear the undead as appropriately their characters would. It's not meant to accurately reflect what undead can do. It's primarily an OOC consideration. So as distinctive to D&amp;D as it is, I would just ignore it in terms of translating the character.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I think all the previous comments are spot on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T22:55:41-07:00","id":1538225,"title":"","content":"Strahd Von Zarovich is a very terrifying character in D&amp;D. After looking at his stats throughout the editions of the game, I've come up with the following notes:<ul><li>Strahd has around 4 dots in all physical attributes; regardless of edition. Likewise his Intelligence is straight up maxed to 5.</li> <li>He would possess 5 dots in Protean, at least 3 into Animalism and Presence, and at least 2 into Dominate.</li> <li>Dude is a 9th-level spellcaster in nearly all editions; meaning he would possess several dots in various forms of Thaumaturgy, Necromancy, and other forms of blood magics.</li> <li>He would have flaws relating to his weakness to invitations and running water. The water in particular would be similar to being in sunlight for him as is the case for all vampires in D&amp;D.</li> <li>Dude is straight up an Old-Clan Tzimisce, as he is bound to Ravenloft like Tzimisces are bound to their place of death or birth. That said, Caitiff also works as he doesn't have the traditional need to sleep in dirt.</li> </ul>While vampires in previous editions have &quot;energy drain&quot; effects, this doesn't translate well into VTM and was more of a mechanic rather than traditional lore. Considering he is not a descendent of Caine, he may not have a traditional Generation stat. Due to how the Shadowfell works, Strahd is both ancient and young at the same time. For him, only a few centuries have past; to the rest of the multiverse, millennia have gone by. As a result, any Generation actually works (although I do suggest it be as low as possible).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T23:42:05-07:00","id":1538226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538225#post1538225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Dude is straight up an Old-Clan Tzimisce, as he is bound to Ravenloft like Tzimisces are bound to their place of death or birth. That said, Caitiff also works as he doesn't have the traditional need to sleep in dirt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's less he's Old Clan due to his connection to the Demiplane, and more he's Old Clan because he's so possessive of what belongs to him - &quot;I am the Land&quot;. Barovia is his, its people are his, and he will not suffer anything that threatens them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T07:00:43-07:00","id":1538232,"title":"","content":"Strahd is an amazing character and I think he\u2019d be perfect as an Old Clan Tzimisce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T08:44:25-07:00","id":1538236,"title":"","content":"I can't add anything new here, but will direct interested parties who are unfamiliar with the source material to the novel <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I,_Strahd:_The_Memoirs_of_a_Vampire\" target=\"_blank\"><i>I, Strahd</i>, by P. N. Elrod</a>. The original I6 Ravenloft module can be found, but has not all that much on Strahd himself, beyond a brief description and a stat block; the 5E hardcover <i>Curse of Strahd</i> has more and an expanded stat block, but both of those are focused on the adventure; the novel is all about who he is and why, and is probably already in the &quot;Appendix N&quot; for VtM in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><b>ROLAND VOLZ</b></span><br /> <b>Running: </b><a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/prokopetz/144980905802/invisiblemelonmoose-prokopetz\" target=\"_blank\">1870s Mashup Hero System Home Game</a> | <b>Playing:</b> nothing\u200b<br /> <i>D&amp;D is an elf from Tolkien, a barbarian from Howard, and a mage from Vance fighting monsters from Lovecraft in a room that looks like it might have been designed by Wells and Giger.</i> - TiaNadiezja","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28542-alhazred","name":"AlHazred","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28542_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T11:58:44-07:00","id":1538243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538224#post1538224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">D&amp;D level drain for undead was an artifact of the game designers wanting players to fear the undead as appropriately their characters would. It's not meant to accurately reflect what undead can do. It's primarily an OOC consideration. So as distinctive to D&amp;D as it is, I would just ignore it in terms of translating the character.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I think all the previous comments are spot on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no.<br /> <br /> The undead connection to the Negative Material Plane is what gave them their &quot;level drain&quot; ability, but it also contributed to their other powers, hence why there were examples of vampires who had their connection to the Negative Material Plane strengthened, gaining powers on par with vampires that were much older. Essentially this would be the VtM equivalent of lowering Generation below 7th.<br /> <br /> This planar connection is also why mummies in D&amp;D have &quot;mummy rot&quot; as a touch attack, except despite being undead, they are connected to the Positive Material Plane. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T12:02:41-07:00","id":1538244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlHazred</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538236#post1538236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't add anything new here, but will direct interested parties who are unfamiliar with the source material to the novel <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I,_Strahd:_The_Memoirs_of_a_Vampire\" target=\"_blank\"><i>I, Strahd</i>, by P. N. Elrod</a>. The original I6 Ravenloft module can be found, but has not all that much on Strahd himself, beyond a brief description and a stat block; the 5E hardcover <i>Curse of Strahd</i> has more and an expanded stat block, but both of those are focused on the adventure; the novel is all about who he is and why, and is probably already in the &quot;Appendix N&quot; for VtM in any case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember seeing the advertisements for the upcoming release of that book, back in 1992..... pardon me, I need to yell at a cloud or some kids to get off my lawn. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T13:27:20-07:00","id":1538249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538244#post1538244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember seeing the advertisements for the upcoming release of that book, back in 1992..... pardon me, I need to yell at a cloud or some kids to get off my lawn. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>LOL, I am equally An Old, but I know people who read it only recently and tell me it compares well to modern vampire literature. It probably helped that P. N. Elrod already had a successful vampire series under her belt before she did <i>I, Strahd</i>! I haven't touched the books in decades and have little interest in vampire literature nowadays (or D&amp;D literature) but I remember the tonal shift between that and the other Strahd novels being jarring at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><b>ROLAND VOLZ</b></span><br /> <b>Running: </b><a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/prokopetz/144980905802/invisiblemelonmoose-prokopetz\" target=\"_blank\">1870s Mashup Hero System Home Game</a> | <b>Playing:</b> nothing\u200b<br /> <i>D&amp;D is an elf from Tolkien, a barbarian from Howard, and a mage from Vance fighting monsters from Lovecraft in a room that looks like it might have been designed by Wells and Giger.</i> - TiaNadiezja","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28542-alhazred","name":"AlHazred","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28542_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T13:31:54-07:00","id":1538250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538243#post1538243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This planar connection is also why mummies in D&amp;D have &quot;mummy rot&quot; as a touch attack, except despite being undead, they are connected to the Positive Material Plane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember this being a back-and-forth thing. Not really relevant to the current conversation, but mummies have been back to Negative Plane creatures since then, but there are &quot;Undying&quot; from Eberron who are similar-but-Positive-Energy creatures, for arcane reasons having more to do with D&amp;Disms than narrative structure or dramatic tension. I'd drop the level drain aspect entirely. Strahd is beefy enough anyway, you don't need it in any iteration of the character to make him scary to characters below superheroic levels of ability.<br /> <br /> For a really distant tie-in, <a href=\"https://www.mtgnexus.com/customcards/9775-curse-of-strahd/73732-strahd-lord-of-b/\" target=\"_blank\">Strahd is now also in <i>Magic: the Gathering</i></a>. At the very least, it should give you some cool art for him. Not sure if they recycled art from the books or went with brand-new art, but MtG usually spends money on good art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><b>ROLAND VOLZ</b></span><br /> <b>Running: </b><a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/prokopetz/144980905802/invisiblemelonmoose-prokopetz\" target=\"_blank\">1870s Mashup Hero System Home Game</a> | <b>Playing:</b> nothing\u200b<br /> <i>D&amp;D is an elf from Tolkien, a barbarian from Howard, and a mage from Vance fighting monsters from Lovecraft in a room that looks like it might have been designed by Wells and Giger.</i> - TiaNadiezja","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28542-alhazred","name":"AlHazred","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28542_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T14:18:00-07:00","id":1538255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlHazred</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538250#post1538250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember this being a back-and-forth thing. Not really relevant to the current conversation, but mummies have been back to Negative Plane creatures since then, but there are &quot;Undying&quot; from Eberron who are similar-but-Positive-Energy creatures, for arcane reasons having more to do with D&amp;Disms than narrative structure or dramatic tension. I'd drop the level drain aspect entirely. Strahd is beefy enough anyway, you don't need it in any iteration of the character to make him scary to characters below superheroic levels of ability.<br /> <br /> For a really distant tie-in, <a href=\"https://www.mtgnexus.com/customcards/9775-curse-of-strahd/73732-strahd-lord-of-b/\" target=\"_blank\">Strahd is now also in <i>Magic: the Gathering</i></a>. At the very least, it should give you some cool art for him. Not sure if they recycled art from the books or went with brand-new art, but MtG usually spends money on good art.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's one I think they took from the books, the others seem to be brand new. They stayed with the current design for the character, but in the books there's very little good images with that design, many ended up being horrendous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T16:24:29-07:00","id":1538261,"title":"","content":"Is there any characters from other settings that you would love to adapt in this setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T18:39:56-07:00","id":1538268,"title":"","content":"Mechanical conversions of Strahd seem boring to me. D&amp;D and VtM have very different mechanics, and what you would give a vampire meant to be the final boss in an adventure in D&amp;D is very different than what you would give an elder NPC for VtM.<br /> <br /> What is more interesting is deciding how to make him fit into the setting which is very different. What's cool is his motivations and personal history. That's why people like the character. He has gravitas and he's tragic despite being an absolute badass and monster.<br /> <br /> First, let's acknowledge Strahd is just Dracula by another name (and purposefully so). He was a nobleman who lead his people in war against an invading enemy and later cursed to be a vampire. That wasn't a problem for Ravenloft. But the World of Darkness already has a Dracula so much of his backstory is already taken. I'd probably just make him a member of the Wallachian boyars who served under Vlad and fought for him against the Turks. Vlad is probably his sire, giving him the embrace soon after he became a vampire so that he had a trusted ally.<br /> <br /> Second, we can't use the name because it's nonsense. Strahd is made up. &quot;Von&quot; denotes a German noble, but Zarovich sounds like something Slavic. Perfectly fine nonsense name for D&amp;D. Doesn't make sense in the WoD which is our world. The best thing is probably to just create a brand new Romanian name that passes the smell test. However, I could be fine with the character having a &quot;vampire name&quot; like &quot;Strahd&quot;. After all, what kind of name is &quot;Lodin&quot;? But if I was ever going to introduce this character into a chronicle I ran, I wouldn't use that name at all.<br /> <br /> Third, the key to Strahd is the origin involving his younger, handsome brother Sergei and the young girl he loves, Tatiana, and Strahd being a middle aged man who spent his entire life in war now wanting the youth and love he gave up. That can be kept entirely with little change. Except that after killing his brother, declaring his love for Tatiana, she committing suicide in grief, and getting killed himself, it was Vlad who turned him into a vampire because he just couldn't see his friend die like that.<br /> <br /> Fourth, he obviously needs some kind of Flaw that includes the ghost of his brother and his search for the reincarnated Tatiana (which may simply be a case of a lookalike rather than actual reincarnation). He desperately wants to find a new &quot;Tatiana&quot; and embrace her so she'll love him and be his for eternity. And he is continually thwarted by the ghost of Sergei helping hunters protect &quot;Tatiana&quot;. Whether &quot;Sergei&quot; is actually a wraith or something else, I'll leave to the ST.<br /> <br /> Fifth, in terms of sects, he's mostly likely a member of the Old Clan Tzimisce in the Oradea League as others have said, but he could also be at home in the Inconnu or True Black Hand. Probably should have been a student in the Scholomance like Dracula. Koldunic Sorcery plus some well known, ancient Paths is fine.<br /> <br /> Sixth, his pacts with the Vistani are probably best done with some Ravnos sorcerer who has Ravnos childer who wander the world and report back to grandma if they ever find someone who looks like Tatiana. These Ravnos could very well have been Roma when mortal, but that's not necessary. The head Ravnos likely owe's Strahd some lifeboon that he can call it in for something like this - it binds her and her childer and further lineage, but it is so inconsequential a favor even in perpetuity it's not much of a burden.<br /> <br /> Seventh, instead of living alone like Dracula or having brides, I'd probably just give him a household staff of ghouls or dominated servants. They keep up the place in case any mortals find their way there, and they go with him when he voyages to somewhere else. To explain why he was not bothered during the Communist era, I'd probably just give him some high level of Obfuscate that confuses people as to whether that castle is inhabited.<br /> <br /> Instead of making him some kind of prisoner in his domain, I'd just have that it prefers to dwell there. Like Dracula, he's prepared to leave his castle and travel the world if it fits his plans (find Tatiana). If I'm going to use him in a chronicle, I'll want him to be able to come to my chronicle's city so the PCs can interact with him. Well known that he's the childe of Dracula himself and that he has never sired another vampire. I'd also make it known he's single handedly destroyed several Sabbat packs who attacked him over the years. That will establish his fighting cred, and it makes sense that a solitary Old Clan Tzimisce who mostly stays in the same place would eventually attract Sabbat packs to diablerize him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T19:11:00-07:00","id":1538273,"title":"","content":"I actually did this for a V20 Sabbat chronicle once. And yes, we rejected the entire metaplot to do this before you ask.<br /> <br /> Strahd Von Zarovich was a member of Old Clan Tzimisce who had befriended several Cappadocian elders and was able to learn Necromancy in the Dark Ages<br /> <br /> After the Giovanni successfully purged the Cappadocians, an outraged Strahd joined the Sabbat when he learned of the nascent Camarilla's truce with the Giovanni usurpers.<br /> <br /> He became a stalwart conservative elder within the Sword of Caine and eventually became the Archbishop of West Virginia by the start of the 20th Century, ruling from his haven in downtown Charleston with an iron fist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 07-08-2024, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T20:16:50-07:00","id":1538277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538268#post1538268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, the key to Strahd is the origin involving his younger, handsome brother Sergei and the young girl he loves, Tatiana, and Strahd being a middle aged man who spent his entire life in war now wanting the youth and love he gave up. That can be kept entirely with little change. Except that after killing his brother, declaring his love for Tatiana, she committing suicide in grief, and getting killed himself, it was Vlad who turned him into a vampire because he just couldn't see his friend die like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>One important aspect of Strahd is that he damned himself. He killed his brother as part of a ritual to gain power, and that's what turned him into a vampire. Of course, that doesn't quite tie in with the way vampirism works in WoD. Still, perhaps he could be a Dark Thaumaturgist who have entered into some kind of a pact which involved him selling his soul to a demon, or the Kupala or something similar. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T06:54:36-07:00","id":1538300,"title":"","content":"A couple of notes:<br /> <br /> 1. Strahd actually could be a couple of other Clans that work well for him: Gangrel, Ventrue, Tremere, or even Toreador. I think he actually works really well as a Cappadocian given his pact with &quot;Death&quot; (now Vampyr).<br /> <br /> 2. You could also make the Life Drain attack as a Mortis one, inflicting permanent health damage to someone unless they are a vampire themselves. Which means that vampires would have an easier time against him.<br /> <br /> 3. Strahd having access to Mortis or Necromancy might also explain the kind of Dark Ages abominations you'd find around Barovia. He's definitely got high level Thaumaturgy, though.<br /> <br /> 4. His pact with Death could be metaphorical in this universe, i.e. his sire or he could be transformed by a demon or other spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T13:56:01-07:00","id":1538319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538268#post1538268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is more interesting is deciding how to make him fit into the setting which is very different. What's cool is his motivations and personal history. That's why people like the character. He has gravitas and he's tragic despite being an absolute badass and monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, although I do think working his stats actually helps to flesh out his story in the WoD. I disagree with some details, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538268#post1538268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, let's acknowledge Strahd is just Dracula by another name (and purposefully so). He was a nobleman who lead his people in war against an invading enemy and later cursed to be a vampire. That wasn't a problem for Ravenloft. But the World of Darkness already has a Dracula so much of his backstory is already taken. I'd probably just make him a member of the Wallachian boyars who served under Vlad and fought for him against the Turks. Vlad is probably his sire, giving him the embrace soon after he became a vampire so that he had a trusted ally.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some distinctions from Strahd to Dracula that I think shouldn't be overlooked. First and foremost, his link to the land.<br /> <br /> I don't think at all that Strahd works outside his home. It is not just about he being a prisoner, but most of his gravitas as a villain comes from how thoroughly he is connected to Barovia. Remember, Strahd isn't linked to Barovia because he's a Darklord, instead it was the concept of a Darklord that was created to both explain and replicate Strahd's link to the land.<br /> <br /> Other than that, although less relevant, there's his role as an original vampire. He's D&amp;D's Caine, and overall relevant for being self-created. Since we already have Tremere and Nagaraja, I don't think it's too farfetched to have him as the progenitor of a similar Bloodline, maybe with help from other vampires, but not Embraced.<br /> <br /> Strahd isn't simply a boss in the expanded setting, he is the supernatural Prince of his domain, whose command is both overt and covert, secular and mystical, monstrous yet legitimate. I think this makes for an excellent Prince for whatever city or domain the PCs live in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538268#post1538268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fourth, he obviously needs some kind of Flaw that includes the ghost of his brother and his search for the reincarnated Tatiana (which may simply be a case of a lookalike rather than actual reincarnation). He desperately wants to find a new &quot;Tatiana&quot; and embrace her so she'll love him and be his for eternity. And he is continually thwarted by the ghost of Sergei helping hunters protect &quot;Tatiana&quot;. Whether &quot;Sergei&quot; is actually a wraith or something else, I'll leave to the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>The obsession with the lost Tatiana could be his Bloodline weakness. You obsess over a person from your past, and after some time without contact you start to see this person on others, as a &quot;reincarnation&quot;.<br /> <br /> Other unique traits could be side effects from the magic that turned him into a vampire, curses and blessings only meant for him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538268#post1538268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sixth, his pacts with the Vistani are probably best done with some Ravnos sorcerer who has Ravnos childer who wander the world and report back to grandma if they ever find someone who looks like Tatiana. These Ravnos could very well have been Roma when mortal, but that's not necessary. The head Ravnos likely owe's Strahd some lifeboon that he can call it in for something like this - it binds her and her childer and further lineage, but it is so inconsequential a favor even in perpetuity it's not much of a burden.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a pact with something other than a vampire would be more interesting, although the Ravnos are a good choice. But something that at least pass for human would make for a more interesting partnership.<br /> <br /> Even not using their full splat, Changelings strike me as a good twist to keep the character from being just a regular vampire lord.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538268#post1538268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seventh, instead of living alone like Dracula or having brides, I'd probably just give him a household staff of ghouls or dominated servants. They keep up the place in case any mortals find their way there, and they go with him when he voyages to somewhere else. To explain why he was not bothered during the Communist era, I'd probably just give him some high level of Obfuscate that confuses people as to whether that castle is inhabited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlike Dracula, Strahd always had many servants, this isn't a new thing for him. And he does have childe, just not the one he wants more. His obsession may work in such a way that if he manages to Embrace his target, the illusion goes away, just to begin anew with another.<br /> <br /> It may also be that he doesn't want to turn Tatiana to begin with, but instead desires her love as a living person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T07:03:24-07:00","id":1538430,"title":"","content":"My fellow nerds, you\u2019ve made excellent points and cogent suggestions, but let me be facetious - in a whole game full of vampires Strahd Von Zarovich is just another fang at the bloodbath unless you have the good sense to make him a creature that only LOOKS like a vampire because it has deliberately adopted the style, as well as the identity, of a vampire so fictional he comes from an actual Fantasy setting (Note the capital \u2018F\u2019).<br /> <br /> Whether this is for it\u2019s very own amusement or for the sake of confusing Vampire elders (Who, with the possible exception of the Toreador, presumably haven\u2019t kept an especially close eye on pop culture since Mozart was in the \u2018forthcoming attractions\u2019 section) or both is, of course, the question.<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Actually, the most appropriate use of this identity by a sufficiently powerful entity would almost certainly be to rub Player Character noses in the fact that they almost certainly wanted to BE Strahd Von Zarovich and a much, much farther from such exalted status than they expected to be after becoming actual **** vampires: with this in mind, the mental image of an especially eccentric Toreador elder deciding to **** with some fledgelings occurs to me.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m wondering what sort of supporting cast and crew they\u2019d need to fake all the Master of Ravenloft\u2019s abilities \u2026 (Also, would they go ALL THE WAY and use an actual Castle to set up their very own Dungeon Crawl or would they be forced to employ a mere studio set?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T07:07:24-07:00","id":1538431,"title":"","content":"In any case, I do genuinely feel that translating Strahd Von Zarovich into an actual VAMPIRE THE MASQUERADE character is far, far less entertaining than using him as a (My apologies, THE) DnD Vampire who somehow popped up in the World of Darkness \u2026 or at least someone (or someTHING) who wants you to think they are and is powerful enough to fake it \u2018till you break it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T15:01:41-07:00","id":1538451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538431#post1538431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In any case, I do genuinely feel that translating Strahd Von Zarovich into an actual VAMPIRE THE MASQUERADE character is far, far less entertaining than using him as a (My apologies, THE) DnD Vampire who somehow popped up in the World of Darkness \u2026 or at least someone (or someTHING) who wants you to think they are and is powerful enough to fake it \u2018till you break it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a confession to make that I actually HAVE used Strahd or variants of him in my games.<br /> <br /> Generally, with two ways.<br /> <br /> 1. Adapting him to the game world in the high drama sort of way. A Ventrue Prince who murdered everyone at a wedding for his brother and got Embraced afterward but is STILL salty about the whole thing years later. The PCs end up getting hired by a Pack of Ravnos Antitribu to find evidence of these murders and the event he covered up before discovering that, in fact, its Strahd playing games--right up until his Brother's Wraith starts possessing people to take him out. Also, a Tzimisce fleshcrafter routinely torments him by making a duplicate of his lady love that he dominates into thinking they're Tatyana as part of a generations long headgame with Strahd that the latter believes is destiny.<br /> <br /> 2. Having him as a full Gothic Old Tzimisce vampire in a Gothic Punk univere and playing the contrast for all its worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T17:16:34-07:00","id":1538453,"title":"","content":"After this thread I do plan on using him either in VtM or VtR, with the full Gothic style, but making him the Prince of the city. And I do want to make the whole &quot;he's Strahd XIII, <i>de facto </i>owner of the place&quot;.<br /> <br /> But <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28339\" data-vbnamecard=\"28339\">Atticus Cleanclaw</a>'s idea of someone pretending to be Strahd isn't bad, either. Or even, on a more gonzo game with dimensional travel, why not the <b>actual </b>Strahd?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T09:38:19-07:00","id":1538520,"title":"","content":"Old Clan Tzimisce, with Koldunic Sorcery. Really doubles down on his link to the land, explains some of the abominations he has access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T09:56:26-07:00","id":1538525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538453#post1538453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After this thread I do plan on using him either in VtM or VtR, with the full Gothic style, but making him the Prince of the city. And I do want to make the whole &quot;he's Strahd XIII, <i>de facto </i>owner of the place&quot;.<br /> <br /> But <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28339\" data-vbnamecard=\"28339\">Atticus Cleanclaw</a>'s idea of someone pretending to be Strahd isn't bad, either. Or even, on a more gonzo game with dimensional travel, why not the <b>actual </b>Strahd?</div> </div> </div> </div>May I suggest a Marauder? Hollow One who loved him some fantasy, used it to build his Paradigm, then when what ever event that drove him so crazy that reality stops arguing happened, he got stuck on being Strahd? Enough Life, Spirit and Prime, with a dash of Mind and Time, and you can have someone everyone thinks is a weird vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T14:02:05-07:00","id":1538862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538525#post1538525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> May I suggest a Marauder? Hollow One who loved him some fantasy, used it to build his Paradigm, then when what ever event that drove him so crazy that reality stops arguing happened, he got stuck on being Strahd? Enough Life, Spirit and Prime, with a dash of Mind and Time, and you can have someone everyone thinks is a weird vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019m not very familiar with MAGE, but this would seem to have the \u201cDUNGEONS AND DRAGONS, leeches!\u201d energy I was thinking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T14:08:21-07:00","id":1538863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538215-how-would-we-adapt-strahd?p=1538453#post1538453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After this thread I do plan on using him either in VtM or VtR, with the full Gothic style, but making him the Prince of the city. And I do want to make the whole &quot;he's Strahd XIII, <i>de facto </i>owner of the place&quot;.<br /> <br /> But <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28339\" data-vbnamecard=\"28339\">Atticus Cleanclaw</a>'s idea of someone pretending to be Strahd isn't bad, either. Or even, on a more gonzo game with dimensional travel, why not the <b>actual </b>Strahd?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now here\u2019s a question: how would we translate World of Darkness Cainites into DUNGEONS AND DRAGONS? (Would visiting the Demiplane of Dread oblige them to play by the rules of D&amp;D vampires or would they become something home-brew?).<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, there are very few wrong ways to mix your favourite flavours: I admit to favouring a \u2018High Contrast\u2019 approach mostly because it pays proper respect to The Dungeons &amp; Dragons vampire, a character so influential they built his very own setting around him (In more ways than one).<br /> <br /> Heck, he\u2019s even the namesake of a setting in an entirely different game-line! (You\u2019re not fooling anyone \u2018Innistrad\u2019, you might be your own thing, but you are also the biggest RAVENLOFT fan \u2026 being a whole darned planet, quite literally the biggest).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T16:18:26-07:00","id":1538873,"title":"","content":"I actually have an old homebrew of Cainites to D&amp;D 3.5, for completely unrelated reasons. But Ravenloft being what it is, it certainly could effect any changes the GM deems necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T09:00:06-07:00","id":1538969,"title":"","content":"Not my site, but I will point people <a href=\"https://www.completecompendium.com/appendix/vampire/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for generic vampire information for AD&amp;D and <a href=\"https://www.completecompendium.com/appendix/vampire0/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for Western Vampire specific information, in case anyone is completely unfamiliar with the AD&amp;D version of vampires. .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><b>ROLAND VOLZ</b></span><br /> <b>Running: </b><a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/prokopetz/144980905802/invisiblemelonmoose-prokopetz\" target=\"_blank\">1870s Mashup Hero System Home Game</a> | <b>Playing:</b> nothing\u200b<br /> <i>D&amp;D is an elf from Tolkien, a barbarian from Howard, and a mage from Vance fighting monsters from Lovecraft in a room that looks like it might have been designed by Wells and Giger.</i> - TiaNadiezja","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28542-alhazred","name":"AlHazred","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28542_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}